            <ArticleTitle>A reappraisal of the maternal syndrome associated with hydrops fetalis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A pregnancy complicated by severe rhesus isoimmunization can not only lead to fetal loss but may also be complicated by a rarely described maternal syndrome. The unusual clinical features of one such case and the probable underlying pathophysiology are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
